---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import PageHero from '../components/PageHero.astro';
import { siteConfig } from '../config/site';

const pageUrl = new URL('/privacy/', siteConfig.siteUrl).toString();
const privacySchemas = [
  {
    '@context': 'https://schema.org',
    '@type': 'PrivacyPolicy',
    '@id': `${pageUrl}#privacy`,
    url: pageUrl,
    name: '5 Whys Career Studio Privacy Policy',
    description:
      'Privacy policy for 5 Whys Career Studio, covering local drafting, exports, and contact requests.',
    isPartOf: {
      '@id': 'https://5whys.jonathanrreed.com/#website',
    },
    author: {
      '@type': 'Person',
      name: siteConfig.author.name,
      url: siteConfig.author.url,
    },
  },
];
---

<Base
  title="Privacy"
  description="Read the 5 Whys Career Studio privacy policy, including how career drafts, browser storage, exports, and contact requests are handled."
  breadcrumbs={[
    { label: 'Home', href: '/' },
    { label: 'Privacy', href: '/privacy/' },
  ]}
  structuredData={privacySchemas}
>
  <div class="relative space-y-10 overflow-hidden px-4 pb-16 pt-8 sm:pt-10">
    <section class="mx-auto w-full max-w-6xl">
      <PageHero
        eyebrow="Privacy"
        title="Your career drafts stay under your control."
        description="5 Whys Career Studio is designed as a lightweight browser tool. It does not require accounts, payments, or a backend database for the core workflows."
      />
    </section>

    <section class="mx-auto w-full max-w-4xl space-y-6">
      <article
        class="rounded-xl border border-border/50 bg-card/50 p-6"
      >
        <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold text-foreground">What the tools store</h2>
        <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-muted-foreground">
          Everything you write, upload, or record stays in your browser on this device: drafts,
          reflections, job postings, your resume, practice recordings, and transcripts. The tools
          save it in browser storage so you can continue later on the same device. None of it is
          sent to a server. The dashboard shows what is stored and has one button that clears
          all of it from this device.
        </p>
      </article>
      <article
        class="rounded-xl border border-border/50 bg-card/50 p-6"
      >
        <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold text-foreground">On-device AI</h2>
        <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-muted-foreground">
          Some tools can suggest wording or questions. Those suggestions are written on your
          device, either by built-in rules or by a model that runs in your browser, and what you
          write is never sent to an AI service by this site. If your browser offers its own model
          and you choose to use it, your browser downloads that model from its maker; your writing
          still stays on your device. No model is downloaded unless you press a button that says
          so. Any wage data and job-title lists are read from this site, and what you type into a
          search is not sent anywhere.
        </p>
      </article>
      <article
        class="rounded-xl border border-border/50 bg-card/50 p-6"
      >
        <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold text-foreground">Exports and contact</h2>
        <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-muted-foreground">
          Files you export are created for your use. If you contact the project by email, the
          message is used to respond to your request and improve the tools.
        </p>
      </article>
      <article
        class="rounded-xl border border-border/50 bg-card/50 p-6"
      >
        <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold text-foreground">Requests</h2>
        <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-muted-foreground">
          For privacy questions or deletion requests related to direct messages you sent, email
          <a
            class="font-semibold text-foreground [overflow-wrap:anywhere] hover:text-accent"
            href="mailto:contact@JonathanRReed.com">contact@JonathanRReed.com</a
          >.
        </p>
      </article>
    </section>

    <section class="mx-auto w-full max-w-4xl">
      <p class="eyebrow eyebrow-accent mb-5 border-t border-border/40 pt-10">
        Good to know
      </p>
      <div class="space-y-4 text-base leading-relaxed text-muted-foreground">
        <p>
          Browser storage is device specific. If a tool saves draft material locally, it is intended
          to help you continue on the same device and browser, not to sync a profile across
          accounts. Clearing site data, using private browsing, or switching devices can remove
          local drafts and settings.
        </p>
        <p>
          On a shared or lab computer, anyone who uses the same browser after you can open the
          dashboard and read what you wrote. Before you leave, press "Clear everything on this
          device" on the dashboard, or do your work in a private window, which forgets it when you
          close it. A backup file you export is plain text: keep it somewhere only you can reach.
        </p>
        <p>
          Schools and younger visitors: the site has no accounts and does not ask who you are, how
          old you are, or where you study. It keeps no record of any visitor, so it holds no
          student records. What a student writes stays on the computer they wrote it on until they
          export or clear it.
        </p>
        <p>
          Avoid pasting confidential employer documents, private client records, medical data,
          financial data, or other sensitive material into any browser tool unless you are
          comfortable keeping that content on your own device. The studio is designed for career
          planning notes, resume drafts, interview stories, and practice material.
        </p>
        <p>
          Exported files and copied text are controlled by the software you choose after leaving the
          page. Treat them like any other career document: review them before sharing, remove
          details that identify people who should stay private, and store important drafts somewhere
          you already trust.
        </p>
        <p>
          The current subprocessor list is published at
          <a class="font-semibold text-foreground hover:text-accent" href="/subprocessors/"
            >5 Whys subprocessors</a
          >.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>
  </div>
</Base>
